{"title":"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) #8</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) #4</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Ahmed is going to the store. One quarter of the way to the store, he stops to talk with Kee. He then continues for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> km and reaches the store. How many kilometers does he travel altogether?\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/5/455817f187f4194c43d66bb187318532e0cc64a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 15 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 16 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 24 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 48 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the total distance that Ahmed travels. From the second sentence of the problem, he traveled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/1/951daa007e3e348f12746def27e6f5f5959f8c8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> going from his starting location to Kee. \n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>We can now see that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e08beebc8416f95a693eb07c7e72ce1114f2b927.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}d + 12 = d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"98\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/f/7dfaaf6f434a6273d35a02250783cf7d94cd1716.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 = d - \\frac{1}{4}d = \\frac{4 - 1}{4}d = \\frac{3}{4}d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"223\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/a/e6a39fb8d9926ab01c14642f8535f690158ea7bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = 12 \\div \\frac{3}{4} = 12 \\times \\frac{4}{3} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"255\" height=\"38\" /> km\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because Ahmed traveled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the distance from his starting location to Kee, we know that he traveled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c4d8f32c50647d38e6d77c3118032475695e173.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 - \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{4 - 1}{4} = \\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"152\" height=\"38\" />. This is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/1/271a4020dd81be029cac9916d80f213262e836c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\times \\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"46\" height=\"38\" />, so he traveled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times as much from Kee to the store compared to where he started to Kee.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/5/235820ed89f9ed54954565f6f7e529e091874bde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{12}{3} = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"55\" height=\"37\" /> km, so his distance from the starting position to Kee was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> km.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>We can now see that he traveled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/a/0ba4545c19bb47c731062444a4a34fc374077ef6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 + 12 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"140\" height=\"30\" /> km.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php